    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Teenage Drug is the second studio album by Irish indie-punk band The Sultans of Ping F.C., originally released in 1994 on Epic Records (with some sources noting a 1993 release). Building on their debut's raucous energy, the album delivers sharp guitar riffs, frenetic rhythms, and the band's signature playful, crass lyrics that blend humor with punk irreverence, as heard in tracks like \"Teenage Drug,\" \"Wake Up And Scratch Me,\" \"Teenage Punks,\" \"Curse,\" and \"Michiko.\" Its rock-infused indie-punk style captures the band's knack for dumb, derivative fun that's impossible to hate, even amid ironic self-awareness.\n\nThe record peaked at #54 on the UK Albums Chart, cementing the Sultans' cult status in the '90s alternative scene for their unpretentious antics and live-wire sound. Recent reissues, such as the 2021 Bandcamp LP and the translucent blue numbered vinyl from Music On Vinyl (forthcoming in 2026), have revived interest, offering high-quality remasters that highlight the album's raw production and enduring appeal to punk enthusiasts.\n\nCritically, Teenage Drug exemplifies the band's strength in turning juvenile themes into infectious anthems, maintaining their reputation as lovable misfits in Irish rock history despite modest commercial success.",
